{
  "action": "In general, a standard system update will make all the necessary changes.",
  "cves": [
    "CVE-2026-74222",
    "CVE-2026-74221",
    "CVE-2026-74225",
    "CVE-2026-74220"
  ],
  "description": "Shahriyar Jalayeri and Mehrun P. Hunter discovered that U-Boot\nincorrectly handled certain NFS READ and NFS READLINK responses. An\nattacker could possibly use this issue to trigger a buffer overflow,\nresulting in a denial of service or arbitrary code execution.\n(CVE-2026-74220, CVE-2026-74221)\n\nShahriyar Jalayeri and Mehrun P. Hunter discovered that U-Boot\nincorrectly handled certain HTTP data storage failures in its lwIP\nimplementation. An attacker could possibly use this issue to trigger a\nuse-after-free, resulting in a denial of service. This issue only\naffected Ubuntu 24.04 LTS and Ubuntu 26.04 LTS. (CVE-2026-74222)\n\nShahriyar Jalayeri and Mehrun P. Hunter discovered that U-Boot did not\nproperly validate certain DHCPv6 option lengths during network boot. An\nattacker could possibly use this issue to trigger out-of-bounds memory\naccess, resulting in a denial of service. This issue only affected\nUbuntu 24.04 LTS and Ubuntu 26.04 LTS. (CVE-2026-74225)",
  "id": "USN-8930-1",
  "isummary": "Several security issues were fixed in U-Boot.",
